# The learning curve in the NUMBER OF REFERENCE SOUNDINGS, as one graph.
#
#     cd chtc && mkdir -p logs && condor_submit_dag size.dag
#     ./fetch_results.sh --clean eval_xco2_s90 eval_xco2_s180 eval_xco2_s270
#     python3 experiments/scoring/size_curve.py --out experiments/scoring/tables \
#         --fig latex/figures
#
# WHAT THIS ANSWERS
# -----------------
# Four questions, one picture:
#
#   * a model diagnostic that speaks to generalization rather than to protocol;
#   * whether 47,900 spectra -- 451 scenes -- is enough, next to a mission that takes a
#     million soundings a day and tunes its bias correction on millions of them;
#   * whether the tail of Figure~\ref{fig:scenes} is a sampling artefact. The
#     cluster-balanced experiment tested re-weighting the scenes we have; this tests
#     having more of them;
#   * the conclusion's claim that the binding constraint is the number and spread of
#     distinct scenes. That is a statement about a slope, and this measures it.
#
# A curve that is still falling at 361 scenes says the models are data-limited and that
# simulating more scenes is the fix. One that has flattened says they are not, and the
# limit is the conditioning or the architecture -- in which case the conclusion has to be
# rewritten. Either outcome is publishable; what is not defensible is asserting the slope
# without having measured it.
#
# WHAT IS HELD FIXED. The configuration (the search's winner at 361 scenes, re-searched at
# no size), the trainer, the epoch count, the covariate preset, and the validation and test
# scenes -- group_split_v1's 45 + 45, in every table. Only the training population moves.
# Because the configuration is not re-searched, the small-data points are pessimistic: a
# smaller training set would have selected a smaller model. Say so when the curve is
# quoted.
#
# THE FOURTH POINT IS FREE. k = 361 is the published run: `xco2_bo.npz` in
# results/group_split_v1_cov, already fetched. size_curve.py reads it as the last point.
#
# COST. Three prep jobs (CPU, minutes), six GPU retrains (1-2 h, concurrent, shorter at the
# small sizes) and three scoring jobs (~20 min). Add the profile tasks by uncommenting the
# blocks at the bottom: +6 retrains and +3 scoring jobs each.
#
# Prerequisites, all already in /staging for the published run (./fetch_results.sh --status):
#   oco2_processed_{train,test}.tar.gz, oco2_profile_stats.tar.gz   stage_data.sh
#   oco2_split_v1.tar.gz                                            prep.sub
#   oco2_covariates_v1.tar.gz                                       covariates.sub
#   results/bo25/bo_<study>_best.json                               the search's select nodes

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ the three subsets
JOB prep_s90   prep_size.sub
VARS prep_s90   size="90"
JOB prep_s180  prep_size.sub
VARS prep_s180  size="180"
JOB prep_s270  prep_size.sub
VARS prep_s270  size="270"

# ------------------------------------------------------- XCO2: two models per subset
JOB det_xco2_s90   train_size.sub
VARS det_xco2_s90   study="det_xco2" size="90"
JOB nf_xco2_s90    train_size.sub
VARS nf_xco2_s90    study="nf_xco2"  size="90"
PARENT prep_s90 CHILD det_xco2_s90 nf_xco2_s90

JOB det_xco2_s180  train_size.sub
VARS det_xco2_s180  study="det_xco2" size="180"
JOB nf_xco2_s180   train_size.sub
VARS nf_xco2_s180   study="nf_xco2"  size="180"
PARENT prep_s180 CHILD det_xco2_s180 nf_xco2_s180

JOB det_xco2_s270  train_size.sub
VARS det_xco2_s270  study="det_xco2" size="270"
JOB nf_xco2_s270   train_size.sub
VARS nf_xco2_s270   study="nf_xco2"  size="270"
PARENT prep_s270 CHILD det_xco2_s270 nf_xco2_s270

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ score
JOB eval_xco2_s90  eval_size.sub
VARS eval_xco2_s90  task="xco2" size="90"  det_study="det_xco2" flow_study="nf_xco2"
PARENT det_xco2_s90 nf_xco2_s90 CHILD eval_xco2_s90

JOB eval_xco2_s180 eval_size.sub
VARS eval_xco2_s180 task="xco2" size="180" det_study="det_xco2" flow_study="nf_xco2"
PARENT det_xco2_s180 nf_xco2_s180 CHILD eval_xco2_s180

JOB eval_xco2_s270 eval_size.sub
VARS eval_xco2_s270 task="xco2" size="270" det_study="det_xco2" flow_study="nf_xco2"
PARENT det_xco2_s270 nf_xco2_s270 CHILD eval_xco2_s270

# ------------------------------------------------- the two profile tasks: size_tasks.dag
#
# They are in a DAG of their own rather than here, because the three prep nodes above have
# already run and their archives cannot be overwritten. See chtc/size_tasks.dag.
#
# ------------------------------------------------- (the original sketch, kept for reference)
# The same three sizes on `last4`. Uncomment to add it: the near-surface task is where
# the amortized posterior currently extracts nothing per-sounding (within/floor = 1.001),
# so its curve answers a different question -- whether that is a data limit or a
# conditioning one.
#
# JOB det_last4_s90   train_size.sub
# VARS det_last4_s90   study="det_last4" size="90"
# JOB nf_last4_s90    train_size.sub
# VARS nf_last4_s90    study="nf_last4"  size="90"
# PARENT prep_s90 CHILD det_last4_s90 nf_last4_s90
# JOB eval_last4_s90  eval_size.sub
# VARS eval_last4_s90  task="last4" size="90" det_study="det_last4" flow_study="nf_last4"
# PARENT det_last4_s90 nf_last4_s90 CHILD eval_last4_s90
#
# ... and the same two blocks for 180 and 270.

# A failed node should not stop the others; RETRY 0 for the reason given in balanced.dag.
RETRY ALL_NODES 0

NODE_STATUS_FILE size.dag.status 30
